#{[17592186530374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530374 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d2ff3943-ac10-594c-b82e-a6425e8c3606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186530033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530384 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e55a1031-a1ea-5352-b0ca-33b6092bf496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530407 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fa645345-9bb6-5b6a-b7b1-5257c890c755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "085bdd72-4fe3-54d7-bc86-1b96c914a54e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530420 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{12}+4{a}_{13} \\\\ 5{a}_{21}+{a}_{22}+4{a}_{23} \\\\ 5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{31}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{31}}(5{a}_{31}+{a}_{32}+4{a}_{33})=5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{3}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "08a9562a-8441-5804-8199-2cecfe4f52dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530421 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{3},$ and\n\n- outputs a scalar $f(x)\\in R$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)={x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{3}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{3}}({x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}{x}_{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}({x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}0+3(2) & 1+2 & 3(1)+0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x,\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication. What is the shape of the total derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "173d167b-5e19-5e83-a0ad-faa7a0c92682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530427 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function multiplies a vector by a $3\\times 3$ matrix. Thus, \n\n- it must act on $3$-dimensional column vectors as input, and\n\n- output a $3$-dimensional column vector.\n\nTherefore, $f:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3},$ and the total derivative will be a $3\\times 3$ matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{T}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot x,\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication. What is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b78008a-d228-5f88-9d88-9b7926941425" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530430 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a scalar-valued function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ with respect to a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ is the row vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, writing out the function $f(x)$ where $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{1\\times 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269669" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 3}\\to {R}^{3}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2dd288c1-a4fd-5154-a46e-c65943d99445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530441 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10{a}_{11}-6{a}_{21}-5{a}_{31}\\, & 10{a}_{12}-6{a}_{22}-5{a}_{32}\\, & 10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂{a}_{33}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{33}}(10{a}_{13}-6{a}_{23}-5{a}_{33})=-5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "439b4dea-3b14-5e08-901c-f0507eee5855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530447 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $3\\times 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "752cfa47-ef2c-5a18-9f32-7e84cd447c33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530479 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{2}$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{2\\times 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the total derivative at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269311" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f,$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere the dot denotes matrix multiplication.\nWhat is the shape of the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b8ee097-f47a-59de-984f-4442445eaee2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530486 #edb/ref 1074 "The total derivative of a vector-valued function $f:R\\to {R}^{m}$ with respect to a scalar $x$ is the column vector\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂x}\\end{aligned}]\\in {R}^{m\\times 1}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the function \n\n- acts on a scalar $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- outputs a vector $f(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the total derivative will be a column vector of shape $3\\times 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269667" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $f:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]A.\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0562d85-9065-5ae6-9356-9eba869acb60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530498 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31} & 5{a}_{12}+{a}_{22}-2{a}_{32}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{a}_{32}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{32}}(5{a}_{11}+{a}_{21}-2{a}_{31})=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530513 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530513 #edb/ref 1069 "q-269512" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530513 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530513 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f:R\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ {x}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186530513 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb5a1bbc-92e2-569a-8c18-7d0fed7e610f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921865305